    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0309" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/1528: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-09T16:00:00+01:00">May 9, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>834. From Murphy from Bernstein<anchor n="62" xml:id="d293-f1"/> for
                        Morgenthau.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d293-f2"/> Reference Madrid’s 1099, April
                    30 to Department.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d293-f3"/> French request transfer
                    additional $300,000 to Malaise at Madrid for expenses maintenance and evacuation
                    to North Africa of French refugees in Spain. Approval of transfer is recommended
                    as it is continuation of program for which transfer of funds was previously
                    approved.</p>
                <pb facs="0310" n="300" xml:id="pg300"/>
                <p>French also request transfer of $200,000 to Madrid for support of French schools
                    in Spain which have rallied to Giraud and are opposing Vichy control. We have no
                    additional information concerning the merits of this latter request.</p>
                <p>To Department. Repeated to Madrid. [Bernstein. Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d293-f1" n="62" xml:id="d293-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably Edward M. Bernstein, Assistant Director of the Division of Monetary
                    Research, Treasury Department.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d293-f2" n="63" xml:id="d293-f2-content">
                <p>Henry Morgenthau, Jr., Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d293-f3" n="61" xml:id="d293-f3-content">
